WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:03.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We spoke backstage. I'm very,
very happy with this look.

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:05.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know what? Are you?
Because I feel like

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:08.908 size:84% position:42%
I should be strapping
Sean Connery to a table

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:12.112
and firing a laser at his balls.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:12.112 --> 00:00:15.281
-It is. It has a very nice,
like, classic Bond villain.

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:17.217 size:78% position:39%
-Yeah, it's like a --
-Like a gentleman --

00:00:17.217 --> 00:00:18.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, you're like
a gentleman villain.

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:22.188
-Yeah, I'm like a jerk
from the '60s who smokes a pipe.

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:23.123 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:25.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know?
That's what I was going for.

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:27.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, well,
mission accomplished.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.495 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:29.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
You --
I mean, let's be honest.

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:32.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
You are -- I know you to be
a lovely person.

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:33.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
-You're very --

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:35.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
"A.P. Bio"
is another example of it.

00:00:35.135 --> 00:00:37.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're very good at --
at playing jerks.

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:39.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:41.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
What is that?
I don't know.

00:00:41.074 --> 00:00:42.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're probably asking me
what that is --

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:44.044 size:81% position:41%
I want you to tell me,
because I don't know.

00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:45.178 size:88% position:44%
Like, if you're my ---
-Maybe, your whole life,

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:48.114
you've been such a good person
and you're so kind to everyone,

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:49.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
and yet you have this tickle
in the back of your head,

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:51.751
and you're like,
"I wish there was somewhere..."

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:52.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know what?
-Yeah.

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:53.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think you're actually
totally right.

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:55.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think I've spent, like,
the majority --

00:00:55.522 --> 00:00:56.289 line:92%
and this is actually true.

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:58.258
And you might not think this
from the characters I play.

00:00:58.258 --> 00:01:02.195
I do consciously try to be
a really, really good person.

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:04.764 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I find people
like the characters I play

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:08.435
so despicable and disgusting
that I have to satirize them.

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:10.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
I have to -- I have --

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:13.206
I'm like, "I have to get inside
your head and figure out, like,

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:16.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
'How can you possibly behave
this way?'"

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:18.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I have to make it funny --
otherwise, I'll go crazy.

00:01:18.645 --> 00:01:21.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-You -- You --

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:22.482 line:92%
For those who don't know,

00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:25.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
you are a Harvard professor
who's fallen from grace

00:01:25.785 --> 00:01:29.089 size:75% position:38%
who is now teaching,
in Toledo, A.P. Bio.

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:30.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yep, mm-hmm.
-One of the things

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:33.793
that's been great about the show
is the kids, the classroom --

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:35.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
they're incredible actors.
-They are.

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:36.930 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And the longer
the show's been on,

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:37.764 line:92%
the more you get to know them.

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:38.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you also
get to work with friends,

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:41.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
as far as like Patton Oswalt
and Paula Pell.

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:43.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
That just must make work
so much fun.

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:45.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's kind of a dream job.
-Yeah.

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:46.206 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Not gonna lie.

00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:47.474 line:92%
It's amazing to be on a show

00:01:47.474 --> 00:01:50.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
with such smart, funny,
incredibly talented people.

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:53.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
And being onscreen
with those people is fun --

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:55.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
being offscreen
is maybe even more fun...

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:56.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-...when you're sitting around

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:57.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you kind of say and do
anything.

00:01:57.817 --> 00:01:59.519 size:75% position:38%
-[ Chuckling ] Yeah?
-That's where, like,

00:01:59.519 --> 00:02:00.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
the gloves really come off.

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:01.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:04.023 line:92%
It's -- Yeah, it's pretty great.

